=item surface - SDL3::Surface object or undef. the SDL_Surface structure to query.

=back

Returns boolean: true if the surface has a color key, false otherwise.

Since: This function is available since SDL 3.2.0.

=head2 SDL_GetSurfaceColorKey

  my $result = SDL_GetSurfaceColorKey($surface, $key);

C: C<< _Bool SDL_GetSurfaceColorKey(SDL_Surface * surface, Uint32 * key) >>

Get the color key (transparent pixel) for a surface.

The color key is a pixel of the format used by the surface, as generated by SDL_MapRGB().

If the surface doesn't have color key enabled this function returns false.

It is safe to call this function from any thread.

=over

=item surface - SDL3::Surface object or undef. the SDL_Surface structure to query.

=item key - reference to a scalar holding unsigned integer, pointer object or undef. a pointer filled in with the transparent pixel.

