Returns boolean: true on success or false on failure; call SDL_GetError() for more information.

Since: This function is available since SDL 3.2.0.

=head2 SDL_SetSurfaceColorMod

  my $result = SDL_SetSurfaceColorMod($surface, $r, $g, $b);

C: C<< _Bool SDL_SetSurfaceColorMod(SDL_Surface * surface, Uint8 r, Uint8 g, Uint8 b) >>

Set an additional color value multiplied into blit operations.

When this surface is blitted, during the blit operation each source color channel is modulated by the appropriate color value according to the following formula:

`srcC = srcC * (color / 255)`

This function can be called on different threads with different surfaces.

=over

=item surface - SDL3::Surface object or undef. the SDL_Surface structure to update.

=item r - unsigned integer. the red color value multiplied into blit operations.

=item g - unsigned integer. the green color value multiplied into blit operations.

=item b - unsigned integer. the blue color value multiplied into blit operations.

=back

Returns boolean: true on success or false on failure; call SDL_GetError() for more information.

Since: This function is available since SDL 3.2.0.

